{"name":"Extinct","hex":"#9490b2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"extinct","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of fire, etc.: no longer alight; of a light, etc.: no longer shining; extinguished, quenched.","Of feelings, a person's spirit, a state of affairs, etc.: put out, as if like a fire; quenched, suppressed.\n\nOf customs, ideas, laws and legal rights, offices, organizations, languages, etc.: no longer existing or in use; defunct, discontinued, obsolete; specifically, of a title of nobility: no longer having any person qualified to hold it."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Synonym of extinguish.\n To stop (fire, etc.) from burning; also, to stop (light, etc.) from shining; to put out, to quench.\n\n To kill (someone).\n To put an end to (something) completely; to annihilate, to destroy.\n\n To cause (an animal or plant species) to die out completely or become extinct (adjective etymology 1 sense 2.3).","To stop (fire, etc.) from burning; also, to stop (light, etc.) from shining; to put out, to quench."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extinct"}],"entries":[{"title":"Extinction","blocks":[{"text":"Extinction is the termination of a species via the death of its last member. A taxon may become functionally extinct before the death of its last member if it loses the capacity to reproduce and recover. As a species' potential range may be very large, determining this moment is difficult, and is usually done retrospectively. This difficulty leads to phenomena such as Lazarus taxa, where a species presumed extinct abruptly \"reappears\" after a period of apparent absence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Thylacinus_Cynocephalus.jpg/330px-Thylacinus_Cynocephalus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extinction","wikidata":"Q123509"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Museum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg/500px-Museum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Museum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg/1280px-Museum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Museum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg/500px-Museum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Palaeotherium is an example of an extinct genus that is only recorded from fossil records before the existence of hominids.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseum_of_Natural_History_Palaeotherium_magnum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Darwin%27s_finches_by_Gould.jpg/500px-Darwin%27s_finches_by_Gould.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Darwin%27s_finches_by_Gould.jpg/1280px-Darwin%27s_finches_by_Gould.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Darwin%27s_finches_by_Gould.jpg/500px-Darwin%27s_finches_by_Gould.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADarwin's_finches_by_Gould.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/LepidodendronOhio.jpg/500px-LepidodendronOhio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/LepidodendronOhio.jpg/1280px-LepidodendronOhio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wi